{
  "test_name": "memory_tools_001",
  "test_file": "data/benchmark/tests/memory_tools/memory_tools_001.json",
  "description": "Memory tools test case 1. Tests that agents can retrieve information from memory and inbox emails to perform complex email tasks. Session 1: 5 memory setup queries. Session 2: 5 emails inserted into inbox. Session 3: 5 reply/forward/send email queries requiring both memory and email information.",
  "session_id": "bench_b51ce4ca",
  "timestamp": "2025-11-03T12:00:00",
  "overall_success": false,
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "user_message": "Note that I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam",
      "agent_response": "Thanks — noted. Total study time: 9.5 hours (3 + 4 + 2.5).\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this note? Options:\n- Send an email reporting these hours (tell me the recipient and whether to send now or save as a draft).\n- Save it as a draft in your drafts folder (tell me a recipient or say “personal log”).\n- Forward/report it to a study group or mentor (tell me the recipient).\n- Just keep it here / no action.\n\nIf you want to send or draft, pick one of these templates (or ask for a custom one) and tell me the recipient and whether to send now or save as a draft.\n\nTemplate — formal (to professor/coach):\nSubject: Study hours update\nBody: Hi [Name], I wanted to update you on my exam preparation this week. I studied 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday — a total of 9.5 hours. Please let me know if you have any feedback or recommendations. Thanks, [Your Name]\n\nTemplate — informal (to study group):\nSubject: Study time this week\nBody: Hey team — quick update: I put in 3 hours (Mon), 4 hours (Tue), and 2.5 hours (Wed) for the exam — 9.5 hours total. How’s everyone else doing?\n\nTemplate — personal log:\nSubject: Study log — week of [date]\nBody: Mon: 3h; Tue: 4h; Wed: 2.5h — Total: 9.5h.\n\nWhich action and template do you want me to use, and who should I send/save it to?",
      "duration_s": 13.032,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "user_message": "I want you to remember that I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved this in your memory.\n\nDetails I recorded:\n- Medication taken at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM today\n- Morning reading: 120/80\n- Evening reading: 118/78\n\nWould you like me to do anything with this entry?\n- Save it as a health log draft (I can create a draft email titled “Blood pressure log — [date]”)\n- Send or forward it to your doctor/caregiver (tell me the recipient and whether to send now or save as a draft)\n- Set a reminder to take meds at those times (or a recurring reminder)\n- Nothing else — just keep it here\n\nIf you want to send it, I can use this quick template:\nSubject: Daily blood pressure log\nBody: Hi [Name], today I took my blood pressure medication at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM. Readings: 120/80 (AM), 118/78 (PM). Let me know if you want more details. Thanks, [Your Name]\n\nWhich would you like?",
      "duration_s": 10.481,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "user_message": "Save this to memory: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved that to your memory.\n\nRecorded details:\n- Breakfast: oatmeal with berries\n- Lunch: chicken salad\n- Dinner: salmon with vegetables\n(date: today)\n\nWould you like me to do anything else with this entry?\n- Save it as a nutrition log draft email (I can create one titled “Daily food log — [date]”)\n- Send/forward it to a nutritionist or caregiver (tell me the recipient)\n- Add calories or portion sizes\n- Start a daily food tracking note\n- Nothing else — just keep it here\n\nWhat would you like?",
      "duration_s": 7.472,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "user_message": "Note that I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved this to memory.\n\nRecorded details:\n- Water: 6 glasses (48 oz total) — about 8 oz per glass\n(date: today)\n\nWould you like me to do anything with this entry?\n- Save it as a hydration log draft (I can create a draft titled “Hydration log — [date]”)\n- Send or forward it to someone (tell me the recipient and whether to send now or save as a draft)\n- Add this to a weekly hydration summary or tracker\n- Set a daily reminder to meet a water goal\n- Nothing else — just keep it here\n\nIf you want to send or draft, here’s a quick template I can use:\nSubject: Daily hydration log\nBody: Hi [Name], today I drank 6 glasses of water (48 oz total). Thanks, [Your Name]\n\nWhich action would you like?",
      "duration_s": 10.499,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "user_message": "Note that I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved this to your memory.\n\nRecorded details (date: today unless you tell me otherwise):\n- Business lunch: $85\n- Parking: $45\n- Train ticket (client meeting): $120\n- Total: $250\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this entry?\n- Create a draft expense email (tell me recipient or say “accounting”)\n- Send an expense email now (tell me recipient and whether to attach receipts)\n- Save it as a personal expense log/draft\n- Add it to a weekly/monthly expense summary\n- Forward it to your manager or accountant (tell me who)\n- Nothing else — just keep it here\n\nIf you want an email, pick a template:\n- Formal (to accounting/finance)\n  Subject: Expense report — [date]\n  Body: Hi [Name], please find my expenses for [date]: Business lunch $85; Parking $45; Train ticket (client meeting) $120. Total: $250. Receipts attached (if applicable). Thanks, [Your Name]\n\n- Informal (to manager)\n  Subject: Expenses from client meeting\n  Body: Hey [Name], I spent $85 on lunch, $45 parking, and $120 on train fare for the client meeting — $250 total. Let me know if you need receipts.\n\nWhich action and template do you want, and who should I send/save/forward it to? Or should I just keep it recorded?",
      "duration_s": 12.759,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "step_type": "start_new_session",
      "description": "Start new session to insert emails into inbox",
